Start by comparing the current market cycle to previous bull/bear cycles. Identify similarities and differences, focusing on factors such as interest rates, inflation, and economic growth. Determine the stage of the current market cycle (early, mid, late). If it is identified as a mid or late stage bull market, reduce the sentiment slightly (anticipating a potential correction). Conversely, if it's identified as an early stage bull market, assign a positive sentiment. Use length and steepness of the market's last decline to determine sentiment and conviction.